A complete multi-layer diagnostic pass over the ospf_enterprise_static topology found no fault. The user's report that "the other building has VANISHED" could not be reproduced or traced to any live mechanism.

**Affected component:** None identified.

**Mechanism:** N/A — the network is operating normally in every observable dimension. The topology-wide reachability scan showed 0% packet loss on all sampled paths. A targeted cross-building probe (host_1_1_1_1 → host_2_1_1_1, 10.2.1.2) returned 4/4 packets with 0% loss and sub-5 ms RTT. The OSPF control plane is fully converged across all six FRR routers with complete Full adjacencies and nine routes each. Both host subnets (10.1.1.0/24 and 10.2.1.0/24) are reachable from each other and from the server zone. DNS resolves all four web hostnames correctly from both building hosts, and HTTP returns 200 OK from all four web servers in both directions.

**Localization:** Infrastructure sweep confirmed no ACL drop rules, no misconfigured addressing, no static ARP entries, and no resolver divergence. L2 snapshot shows no real MAC conflicts (only normal null-MAC Linux tunnel pseudo-interfaces). Pressure sweep found no stress tools, CPU saturation, or socket exhaustion on any device.

**Root cause:** No anomaly exists in the live network; the user's reported symptom is unconfirmed and leaves no mechanism or historical trace.

**Fix:** No corrective action is required. If the problem recurs, capture the specific destination names or IPs failing at the time of the complaint to enable targeted diagnosis.
